            The x-intercept is where the line and the x-axis meet; in other words, the value of x when y = 0. In this case, the x-intercept is the number of boss fights when Xander has
            $$ y = 0 \text{ magic points} $$
            That means that the x-intercept is the number of bosses that Xander can fight with the mana he stocked up on, which is
            $$ x = 6 \text{ boss fights} $$
            <div id='manaXint' class='jxgbox square-graph' <%- graphOpts %> ></div>

            <p>So the x-intercept in this case represents the number of bosses that Xander can fight before having to replenish his mana.</p>
        </div>

